--TEST--
`Core\Program::implementing` and `implementingWith` refuse a listed class whose `private` or `protected` constructor the call cannot reach, as a written `new` there is refused (`rule:programs/implementing`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Open` has a public constructor and is accepted. `Hidden` and `Guarded` hide
// their constructors, so each call that lists them is refused where it is
// written: two classes for `implementing` and one for `implementingWith`.
interface Plugin {
    public function name(): string;
}

class Open implements Plugin {
    public function constructor() { }
    public function name(): string { return "open"; }
}

class Hidden implements Plugin {
    private function constructor() { }
    public function name(): string { return "hidden"; }
}

class Guarded implements Plugin {
    protected function constructor() { }
    public function name(): string { return "guarded"; }
}

interface Single {
    public function name(): string;
}

class Lonely implements Single {
    private function constructor() { }
    public function name(): string { return "lonely"; }
}

echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::implementing<Plugin>()), "\n";
var $rows = Core\Program::implementingWith<Single, {order: int}>();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0471]: `Guarded::constructor()` is `protected`, so only `Guarded` and the classes that extend it reach it
%A
error[E0471]: `Hidden::constructor()` is `private`, so only `Hidden`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error[E0471]: `Lonely::constructor()` is `private`, so only `Lonely`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
